# ============================================================
# Powder XRD pattern -- SPARSE PEAK LIST variant (2 columns, same model).
# ============================================================
# Same 2-column (2theta, intensity) model as experimental.dat -- but only
# the peak maxima are listed, e.g. as you'd copy out of a published table
# or an indexed reference pattern, instead of a full continuous scan.
#
# core/xrd.py::looks_like_peak_list() auto-detects this shape (highly
# UNEVEN spacing between points -- some peaks close together, big empty
# gaps elsewhere) and Gaussian-broadens it (FWHM=0.1 deg, same convention
# the simulated pattern itself uses) before comparing, so it's on equal
# footing with a real continuous scan instead of being cubic-interpolated
# straight through the gaps (README section 3.4/1.4). Pass
# --raw-experimental to compare it exactly as-is instead.
#
# Same real peaks as experimental.dat's own 9 strongest reflections
# (extracted with scipy.signal.find_peaks) -- (111), (220), (311), (422),
# (331), (400), plus 3 higher-angle reflections beyond this workflow's
# default 0-90 deg --two-theta-range.
# ============================================================
  28.330    100.000
  47.110     47.434
  55.890     24.408
  68.830      5.224
  76.040      7.023
  87.610      8.218
  94.480      4.289
 106.130      2.366
 113.430      4.133
